"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1605,"Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashar, who narrated to us Yahya ibn Sa'id, who narrated to us Ismail, who narrated to us Qais, on the authority of Abu Mas'ud Uqbah ibn Amr (RA). And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la, who narrated to us al-Mu'tamir, who said: I heard Ismail, on the authority of Qais, who reported that Abu Mas'ud Uqbah ibn Amr (RA) said to us. And narrated to us Salm ibn Junadah, who narrated to us Waki', on the authority of Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of Qais ibn Abi Hazim, on the authority of Abu Mas'ud (RA), who said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, ""Indeed I am delayed from the Fajr prayer because of so-and-so, who makes the prayer lengthy for us."" The narrator of this chain stated: I never saw the Prophet (ﷺ) more angry during a sermon than he was on that day. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""O people, verily among you are those who drive people away from the prayer. So whoever among you leads the people in prayer, let him be brief, for among the congregation are the weak, the elderly, and those with needs."" This is the hadith transmitted via the chain of Bundar (Muhammad ibn Bashar, known by this nickname)."
